data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# Dispatch d002 summary — \\\"greet, tested\\\"\\n\\n## What I did\\n\\n1. Created `src/greet.py` with:\\n   ```python\\n   def greet(name):\\n       return \\\"Hello, {}!\\\".format(name)\\n   ```\\n   `greet(\\\"Alice\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, Alice!\\\"` as required.\\n\\n2. Created `tests/test_greet.py` with two unittest cases:\\n   - `test_normal_name`: `greet(\\\"Alice\\\") == \\\"Hello, Alice!\\\"`\\n   - `test_empty_string`: `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n   The test file inserts `../src` into `sys.path` so `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`\\n   works from the repo root without a package layout.\\n\\n3. Ran the required test command from the repo root (`~/subject`):\\n\\n   ```\\n   $ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n   ..\\n   ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n   Ran 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\n   OK\\n   exit=0\\n   ```\\n\\n   Exit code: **0** — all tests pass, no import errors.\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\n- Branch: `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`\\n- Commit: `b38fc9c` — \\\"Implement greet() with unittest coverage (dispatch d002)\\\"\\n- Files: `src/greet.py`, `tests/test_greet.py` (21 insertions)\\n- Only untracked leftovers are `__pycache__/` directories (bytecode, not committed).\\n\\nAll three dispatch requirements are satisfied. Nothing blocked.\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-summary.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_9","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1788728293,"id":"chatcmpl-f9305fbc22d24da0b08825f8404e8ad2","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

